WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.677
Week 4: Identity, Origin, Numbers, and Time. state origin and profession exchange contact numbers tell dates and times

2
00:00:08.677 --> 00:00:16.841
Mission brief. Complete a registration interview with identity, origin, telephone number, birth date, and appointment time.

3
00:00:16.841 --> 00:00:26.246
Preparation. Select ten useful words, three linking expressions, and two repair phrases. Plan points rather than a memorized paragraph.

4
00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:34.027
Performance. Complete the task once for fluency, review the evidence, then repeat it for greater clarity and accuracy.

5
00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:42.554
After-action review. Record what succeeded, what blocked communication, and the single change that will matter most on the next attempt.

6
00:00:42.554 --> 00:01:04.545
Model language. Soy de los Estados Unidos. — I am from the United States. Mi apellido es Clark. — My last name is Clark. Hoy es el diecinueve de julio. — Today is July nineteenth. Son las tres y cuarto. — It is a quarter past three. ¿A qué hora es la reunión? — What time is the meeting?

7
00:01:04.545 --> 00:01:14.443
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
